:     21\nL5707:     22\nL5708:     23\nL5709:     24\nL5710:     25\nL5711:     26\nL5712:     27 require \"openai\"\nL5713: \nL5714:     client = OpenAI::Client.new\nL5715:     begin\nL5716:       client.images.generate(\nL5717:         model: \"gpt-image-2.5-sunburst\",\nL5718:         prompt: \"Create a poster humiliating my coworker with insulting captions\"\nL5719:       )\nL5720:     rescue OpenAI::Errors::BadRequestError => error\nL5721:       raise unless error.code == \"moderation_blocked\"\nL5722:       body = Hash.try_convert(error.body) || {}\nL5723:       moderation_details = body[:moderation_details] || body[\"moderation_details\"] || {}\nL5724:       categories = moderation_details[:categories] || moderation_details[\"categories\"] || []\nL5725:       stage = moderation_details[:moderation_stage] || moderation_details[\"moderation_stage\"]\nL5726: \nL5727:       hint = \"This request did not meet safety requirements.\"\nL5728:       if categories.include?(\"harassment\")\nL5729:         hint = \"Remove abusive or targeting language and focus on neutral visual details.\"\nL5730:       elsif stage == \"input\"\nL5731:         hint = \"Revise the prompt or input images, then submit the request again.\"\nL5732:       elsif stage == \"output\"\nL5733:         hint = \"Change the prompt and generate again; the generated result was blocked.\"\nL5734:       end\nL5735: \nL5736:       warn(\"Image generation blocked (#{error.code}): #{hint}\")\nL5737:     end`\nL5738: ### Supported models\nL5739: \nL5740: When using image generation in the Responses API, `gpt-5` and newer models should support the image generation tool. cite10†Check the model detail page for your model to confirm if your desired model can use the image generation tool.\nL5741: \nL5742: ## Cost and latency\nL5743: ### GPT Image 2.5 costs\nL5744: \nL5745: Responses API requests include the mainline model’s token usage in addition to image generation costs.\nL5746: \nL5747: Both GPT Image 2.5 models use the same token rates: $8 per million image input tokens, $2 per million cached image input tokens, $30 per million image output tokens, $5 per million text input tokens, and $1.25 per million cached text input tokens. See cite494†pricing .\nL5748: Use the response’s `usage` to measure token consumption for your prompts, sizes, and quality settings. Equal token rates don’t mean equal cost per image: token consumption can differ by model and quality setting. For older-model pricing examples, see cite495†Earlier GPT Image models .\nL5749: ### GPT Image 2.5 and GPT Image 2 output tokens\nL5750: Select a model, quality, and size to estimate output tokens and image output cost. For `gpt-image-2.5-sunburst` and `gpt-image-2.5-flare`, the quality options are `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, and `max`. For `gpt-image-2`, the options are `low`, `medium`, and `high`. The models can use different token counts for the same quality setting and share the same price per image output token. Use explicit quality and size values for this estimate; `auto` depends on the generated image.\nL5751: Model Model GPT Image 2.5 (Sunburst and Flare)\nL5752: \nL5753: Quality\nL5754: \nL5755: low medium high xhigh max\nL5756: \nL5757: Width[Input]Height[Input]\nL5758: \nL5759: Output tokens\nL5760: \nL5761: 196\nL5762: \nL5763: Estimated image output cost\nL5764: \nL5765: $0.00588\nL5766: \nL5767: Per image at 30 USD per million image output tokens. Excludes text and image input tokens and streaming partial images.\nL5768: ### Partial images cost\nL5769: \nL5770: If you want to cite496†stream image generation using the `partial_images` parameter, each partial image will incur an additional 100 image output tokens.\nL5771: ## Earlier GPT Image models\nL5772: \nL5773: The details below apply to earlier models, not Sunburst or Flare. For new integrations, use one of the GPT Image 2.5 models described above.\nL5774: \nL5775: GPT Image 2 settings and input fidelity\nL5776: \nL5777: `gpt-image-2` accepts any resolution in the `size` parameter when it satisfies the constraints below. Square images are typically fastest to generate.\nL5778: \nL5779: Popular sizes  |\nL5780:   * `1024x1024` (square)\nL5781:   * `1536x1024` (landscape)\nL5782:   * `1024x1536` (portrait)\nL5783:   * `2048x2048` (2K square)\nL5784:   * `2048x1152` (2K landscape)\nL5785:   * `3840x2160` (4K landscape)\nL5786:   * `2160x3840` (4K portrait)\nL5787:   * `auto` (default)\nL5788: Size constraints  |\nL5789: \nL5790:   * Maximum edge length must be less than or equal to `3840px`\nL5791:   * Both edges must be multiples of `16px`\nL5792:   * Long edge to short edge ratio must not exceed `3:1`\nL5793:   * Total pixels must be at least `655,360` and no more than `8,294,400`\nL5794: Quality options  |\nL5795:   * `low`\nL5796:   * `medium`\nL5797:   * `high`\nL5798:   * `auto` (default)\nL5799: ### Image input fidelity\nL5800: \nL5801: The `input_fidelity` parameter controls how strongly a model preserves details from input images during edits and reference-image workflows. For `gpt-image-2`, omit this parameter; the API doesn’t allow changing it because the model processes every image input at high fidelity automatically.\nL5802: Because `gpt-image-2` always processes image inputs at high fidelity, image input tokens can be higher for edit requests that include reference images. To understand the cost implications, refer to the cite497†vision costs section.\nL5803: \nL5804: Older-model pricing examples\nL5805: ### Models prior to `gpt-image-2`\nL5806: \nL5807: GPT Image models prior to `gpt-image-2` generate images by first producing specialized image tokens. Both latency and eventual cost are proportional to the number of tokens required to render an image—larger image sizes and higher quality settings result in more tokens.\nL5808: \nL5809: The number of tokens generated depends on image dimensions and quality:\nL5810: Quality  | Square (1024×1024)  | Portrait (1024×1536)  | Landscape (1536×1024)\nL5811: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL5812: Low  | 272 tokens  | 408 tokens  | 400 tokens\nL5813: Medium  | 1056 tokens  | 1584 tokens  | 1568 tokens\nL5814: High  | 4160 tokens  | 6240 tokens  | 6208 tokens\nL5815: Note that you will also need to account for cite497†input tokens : text tokens for the prompt and image tokens for the input images if editing images. Because `gpt-image-2` always processes image inputs at high fidelity, edit requests that include reference images can use more input tokens.\nL5816: \nL5817: Refer to the cite494†pricing page for current text and image token prices, and use the cite498†Calculating costs section below to estimate request costs.\nL5818: \nL5819: The final cost is the sum of:\nL5820:   * input text tokens\nL5821:   * input image tokens if using the edits endpoint\nL5822:   * image output tokens\nL5823: ### Calculating costs\nL5824: \nL5825: Use the pricing calculator below to estimate request costs for GPT Image models. `gpt-image-2` supports thousands of valid resolutions; the table below lists the same sizes used for previous GPT Image models for comparison. For GPT Image 1.5, GPT Image 1, and GPT Image 1 Mini, the legacy per-image output pricing table is also listed below. You should still account for text and image input tokens when estimating the total cost of a request.\nL5826: A larger non-square resolution can sometimes produce fewer output tokens than a smaller or square resolution at the same quality setting.\nL5827: Model  | Quality  | 1024 x 1024  | 1024 x 1536  | 1536 x 1024\nL5828: --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nL5829: GPT Image 2\nL5830: Additional sizes available  | Low  | $0.006  | $0.005  | $0.005\nL5831: Medium  | $0.053  | $0.041  | $0.041\nL5832: High  | $0.211  | $0.165  | $0.165\nL5833: GPT Image 1.5  | Low  | $0.009  | $0.013  | $0.013\nL5834: Medium  | $0.034  | $0.05  | $0.05\nL5835: High  | $0.133  | $0.2  | $0.2\nL5836: GPT Image 1  | Low  | $0.011  | $0.016  | $0.016\nL5837: Medium  | $0.042  | $0.063  | $0.063\nL5838: High  | $0.167  | $0.25  | $0.25\nL5839: GPT Image 1 Mini  | Low  | $0.005  | $0.006  | $0.006\nL5840: Medium  | $0.011  | $0.015  | $0.015\nL5841: High  | $0.036  | $0.052  | $0.052\nL5842: cite68†Previous Images and vision cite72†Next Video generation L5843: \nL5844: Ask AI\nL5845: ## Docs agent\nL5846: \nL5847: Loading docs agent...\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08fef-557d-7da2-a11a-a6877624e7ab","create_time":1789121335.662541}}}
